1
00:03:57,142 --> 00:04:03,142
Enchanted dancing in a magical world!

2
00:07:54,285 --> 00:08:00,285
Barbie in the 12 Dancing Princesses is a animation,
family film directed by Greg Richardson.

3
00:11:51,428 --> 00:11:57,428
King Randolph sends for his cousin, Duchess Rowena, to help turn his daughters,
Princess Genevieve and her eleven sisters, into royal material.

4
00:15:48,571 --> 00:15:54,571
But the Duchess strips the sisters of their fun,
including their favorite pastime: dancing.

5
00:19:45,714 --> 00:19:51,714
When all hope may be lost, the sisters discover a secret passageway to
a magical land where they can dance the night away.

6
00:23:42,857 --> 00:23:48,857
Genevieve (voice), played by Kelly Sheridan.

7
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:46,000
Duchess Rowena (voice), played by Catherine O'Hara.

8
00:31:37,142 --> 00:31:43,142
King Randolph (voice), played by Christopher Gaze.

9
00:35:34,285 --> 00:35:40,285
Ashlyn / Twyla (voice), played by Nicole Oliver.

10
00:39:31,428 --> 00:39:37,428
Blair (voice), played by Jennifer Copping.

11
00:43:28,571 --> 00:43:34,571
Courtney (voice), played by Lalainia Lindbjerg.

12
00:47:25,714 --> 00:47:31,714
Barbie in the 12 Dancing Princesses is a 2006 animated dance film.

13
00:51:22,857 --> 00:51:28,857
It premiered on Nickelodeon on September 10, 2006, and it
was later released to DVD on September 19.

14
00:55:20,000 --> 00:55:26,000
The film was directed by Greg Richardson and loosely based on the
German fairy tale "The Twelve Dancing Princesses".

15
00:59:17,142 --> 00:59:23,142
It is the ninth entry in the Barbie film series and features the
voice of Kelly Sheridan as the Barbie protagonist.

16
01:03:14,285 --> 01:03:20,285
This is the first Barbie film to be distributed by Universal Studios Home Entertainment in North America, to-which Universal's
international subsidiary already handled distribution to the previous films under a deal with Entertainment Rights.

17
01:07:11,428 --> 01:07:17,428
Music for the film was composed by Arnie Roth.

18
01:11:08,571 --> 01:11:14,571
"Shine", the end title song written by Roth, Amy Powers and Rob
Hudnut, was nominated for a 2007 Emmy Award.

19
01:15:05,714 --> 01:15:11,714
The film explores themes of princess, dance,
sibling relationship, magic, ballet.

20
01:19:02,857 --> 01:19:08,857
The tone is lighthearted.
